        "body": "<!-- proofline:finding-series=01a202cc-e753-776d-970f-ceb32d7182ad -->\n**Warning** \u00b7 History emits fractional cursors the console rejects\n\nThis change returns `scheduled_at` as the cursor. SQLite can store a fractional value there, but `--cursor` only accepts integers.\n\nIf a fractional timestamp ends a non-final page, the console rejects the emitted cursor and cannot resume from it.\n\nUse a cursor format that round-trips fractional timestamps without rounding.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Details</summary>\n\nThe only repository caller of `schedule` parses its timestamp as an integer, so no caller supplying a fractional timestamp was found. The scheduling function itself binds the value unchanged, and the schema allows SQLite to retain it as a REAL. Before this change, the cursor came from the integer primary key.\n\n</details>\n\n[View finding in Proofline](https://proofline.sh/orgs/by-id/01a202a0-cd61-7684-99bc-53c775b0de50/reviews/01a202cb-e36b-7316-8580-bd034d371763/findings/01a202cc-e75c-7351-903e-87a99ac3a386)",
